From 79e8032042b004e49fb6f18ecf62d4fe16fd9bc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Minkovsky <dminkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:39:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Read what Android Auto and the Shuffle gate need from core

The library search names the track a spoken play plays (first track found,
else the first track of the first album found) and the album grid's count says
whether the library has a track to shuffle, so Android Auto's lookups and the
Mac menu stop working them out from other values. An album's main release is
its first release, and Android Auto's single lookups read once instead of
keeping a cache of live queries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
